## What happened

Starting in .NET 11 (following the deprecation path begun in earlier releases), `DSA.Create()` throws **`PlatformNotSupportedException`** on macOS. Apple's native crypto libraries (Security.framework / CryptoKit) do not support DSA, and .NET on macOS no longer ships an OpenSSL fallback for this algorithm.

On Linux (OpenSSL) and Windows (CNG) the API still works, which is why only macOS breaks.

## How to fix it

Since you only need to **verify** existing signatures (not generate new ones), the simplest cross-platform fix is to use **BouncyCastle** (or another managed implementation) for DSA verification:

```bash
dotnet add package BouncyCastle.Cryptography
```

Then replace the platform call:

```csharp
using Org.BouncyCastle.Crypto.Parameters;
using Org.BouncyCastle.Crypto.Signers;
using Org.BouncyCastle.Security;

public static bool VerifyDsaSignature(byte[] publicKeyBytes, byte[] message, byte[] signature)
{
    var keyParam = (DsaPublicKeyParameters)PublicKeyFactory.CreateKey(publicKeyBytes);
    var signer = new DsaSigner();
    signer.Init(forSigning: false, keyParam);

    // Decode the DER-encoded signature into (r, s)
    var seq = (Org.BouncyCastle.Asn1.Asn1Sequence)
              Org.BouncyCastle.Asn1.Asn1Object.FromByteArray(signature);
    var r = ((Org.BouncyCastle.Asn1.DerInteger)seq[0]).Value;
    var s = ((Org.BouncyCastle.Asn1.DerInteger)seq[1]).Value;

    // Hash the message (SHA-1 was typical for legacy DSA)
    var digest = Org.BouncyCastle.Security.DigestUtilities.CalculateDigest("SHA-1", message);

    return signer.VerifySignature(digest, r, s);
}
```

## Alternatives

| Option | Trade-off |
|--------|-----------|
| BouncyCastle (managed) | Works everywhere, no native deps |
| Conditional `RuntimeInformation` check + P/Invoke OpenSSL on macOS | More complex, requires `brew install openssl` |
| Target `net11.0-macos` with a `#if` guard that skips DSA on macOS | Only if macOS verification isn't required |

**Recommendation:** BouncyCastle gives you a single code path across all three platforms with no native dependency management.
